From 54ba39e2ded0285509eeaa109f5116458de11c17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 01:12:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player/command: fix subprocess arg type puns that break on
 big-endian
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

cmd_subprocess read capture_size via v.i, but the option is declared
OPT_BYTE_SIZE(v.i64): the truncated read returns the int64's low word
on little-endian (accidentally the right value) and its high word on
big-endian, i.e. 0. With max_size == 0, subprocess_read() discarded
every captured chunk while the exit status stayed valid, so on ppc any
"subprocess" capture came back empty with status 0 — ytdl_hook parsed
an empty stdout and every yt-dlp-resolved URL failed to play.

Same pun class: playback_only's default OPTDEF_INT(1) hands the bool
option type a const int; it copies sizeof(bool) bytes, reading the
int's first byte — true on little-endian, false on big-endian. Point
defval at an actual bool.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GZD3d75hxiZw4SbMayCw1P
---
 player/command.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/player/command.c b/player/command.c
index a5b5e7e6f5..2739916d1e 100644
--- a/player/command.c
+++ b/player/command.c
@@ -6846,7 +6846,10 @@ static void cmd_subprocess(void *p)
         fdctx[fd] = (struct subprocess_fd_ctx) {
             .log = fdlog,
             .talloc_ctx = tmp,
-            .max_size = cmd->args[2].v.i,
+            // capture_size is OPT_BYTE_SIZE(v.i64): reading v.i here returns
+            // the high word on big-endian (= 0), silently discarding all
+            // captured output while the exit status stays valid.
+            .max_size = cmd->args[2].v.i64,
             .msgl = fd == 2 ? MSGL_ERR : MSGL_INFO,
         };
     }
@@ -7772,7 +7775,10 @@ const struct mp_cmd_def mp_cmds[] = {
     { "subprocess", cmd_subprocess,
         {
             {"args", OPT_STRINGLIST(v.str_list)},
-            {"playback_only", OPT_BOOL(v.b), OPTDEF_INT(1)},
+            // The bool option type copies sizeof(bool) bytes from defval, so
+            // an OPTDEF_INT default reads the int's first byte: 1 on little-
+            // endian, 0 on big-endian. Point it at an actual bool.
+            {"playback_only", OPT_BOOL(v.b), .defval = (void *)&(const bool){true}},
             {"capture_size", OPT_BYTE_SIZE(v.i64), M_RANGE(0, INT_MAX),
                 OPTDEF_INT64(64 * 1024 * 1024)},
             {"capture_stdout", OPT_BOOL(v.b), .flags = MP_CMD_OPT_ARG},
-- 
2.43.0

